READ: HF share is power above HALF-NYQUIST of each image's OWN grid. A sharp, properly
sampled image carries real detail there. A LOW value means the pixel grid is finer than
the actual optical detail - the image is soft for its own stated resolution, and its
nominal GSD overstates what the model can actually see.
